<http://data.silknow.org/object/102a81c1-c52b-3f5a-82c4-ce061930a0be>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "John Hungerford Pollen, 'Report on Fancy Furniture (Class 14)', in <i>Reports on the Paris Universal Exhibition, 1867</i>, vol. II  (London 1867), p.300.\n\nWilliam Maskell, <i>Handbook of the Jones Collection in the South Kensington Museum </i>(London 1883), pp.34 and  43.\r\n\r\nCharles Handley-Read, ‘England 1830–1901’ in <i>World Furniture: An Illustrated History</i>, ed. Helena Hayward  (London 1965), p.215.\r\n\r\nSimon Jervis, ‘Gothic at No. 95 Piccadilly: New Light on the Taste of John Jones’, <i>Apollo</i>  XCV no. 121 (March 1972),  pp.206–11. \r\n\r\nSimon Jervis, ‘Ruskin and Furniture’, <i>Furniture History </i>vol. IX (1973), pp.97–109.\r\n\r\nSimon Swynfen Jervis and Dudley Dodd, <i>Roman Splendour, English Arcadia: The English taste for Pietre Dure and  the Sixtus Cabinet at Stourhead</i> (London 2015), p.39.\r\n\r\nMax Donnelly, 'Rossetti, Poynter, and two bookcases commissioned by John Jones at the Victoria and Albert Museum', <i>The Burlington Magazine</i> vol. 158, no. 1363 (October 2016), pp.803–11."@en ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/abe86da1-ecaf-3e06-88fd-0864e6df0857> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "John Hungerford Pollen, 'Report on Fancy Furniture (Class 14)', in <i>Reports on the Paris Universal Exhibition, 1867</i>, vol. II  (London 1867), p.300.\n\nWilliam Maskell, <i>Handbook of the Jones Collection in the South Kensington Museum </i>(London 1883), pp.34 and  43.\r\n\r\nCharles Handley-Read, ‘England 1830–1901’ in <i>World Furniture: An Illustrated History</i>, ed. Helena Hayward  (London 1965), p.215.\r\n\r\nSimon Jervis, ‘Gothic at No. 95 Piccadilly: New Light on the Taste of John Jones’, <i>Apollo</i>  XCV no. 121 (March 1972),  pp.206–11. \r\n\r\nSimon Jervis, ‘Ruskin and Furniture’, <i>Furniture History </i>vol. IX (1973), pp.97–109.\r\n\r\nSimon Swynfen Jervis and Dudley Dodd, <i>Roman Splendour, English Arcadia: The English taste for Pietre Dure and  the Sixtus Cabinet at Stourhead</i> (London 2015), p.39.\r\n\r\nMax Donnelly, 'Rossetti, Poynter, and two bookcases commissioned by John Jones at the Victoria and Albert Museum', <i>The Burlington Magazine</i> vol. 158, no. 1363 (October 2016), pp.803–11."@en .

